<Layout
	title="Affiliate Disclosure — The Wrist Journal"
	description="Affiliate disclosure for The Wrist Journal, including how affiliate links work and how they relate to editorial recommendations."
	pubDate={new Date("2026-08-30")}
>
	<p>
		Some links on The Wrist Journal are affiliate links. If you buy something through one of those links, the site may earn a commission at no extra cost to you.
	</p>

	<p>
		The Wrist Journal participates in the Amazon Associates programme. As an Amazon Associate, I earn from qualifying purchases.
	</p>

	<h2>What This Means for Recommendations</h2>

	<p>
		Affiliate links help support the running of the site, but they do not decide which watches are recommended or what I say about them. A watch does not get a better verdict because a retailer offers an affiliate programme, and an affiliate relationship does not make a weak product worth recommending.
	</p>

	<p>
		Where possible, links are included because they are useful to readers who want to check current pricing or availability. Prices and stock can change after an article is published, so it is always worth checking the final retailer listing before buying.
	</p>

	<p>
		For more on how articles and recommendations are put together, see the <a href="/editorial-policy">Editorial Policy</a>.
	</p>
</Layout>
